{"id":"fulton-one-man-caravan","title":"Robert Fulton Jr: One Man Caravan","who":"Robert Edison Fulton Jr","when":"1932–1933, 18 months","vehicle":"Douglas twin motorcycle","kind":"moto","color":"#78350f","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"One Man Caravan","by":"Robert Edison Fulton Jr","isbn":"1884313051"}],"summary":"A 23-year-old Harvard architecture graduate rides from London to Tokyo, about 25,000 miles, filming 40,000 feet of the world on the way. A night in a Turkish jail, Iraqi bandits avoided, almost shot at in the Khyber Pass, a guest of Indian rajahs. He later invented the Skyhook rescue system.","sources":[{"label":"The Vintagent: Fulton's One Man Caravan","url":"https://thevintagent.com/?p=75298"},{"label":"Common Tread: solo around the world in 1932","url":"https://www.revzilla.com/common-tread/solo-around-the-world-in-1932-the-robert-edison-fulton-jr-story"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Robert Edison Fulton Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Edison_Fulton_Jr."}],"approximate":"Only the main places of the book; the roads and the Asian legs are approximate.","km":15522,"bbox":[-0.1278,28.6274,139.7639,51.5129],"stops":[{"name":"London","place":"London, UK","at":[51.5074,-0.1278],"date":"1932","text":"Off on a borrowed idea: ride round the world and study its buildings.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg/500px-London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg","page":"London","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Vienna","place":"Vienna, Austria","at":[48.2084,16.3725],"text":"Where he had studied architecture.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg/500px-Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg","page":"Vienna","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schoenbrunn_philharmoniker_2012.jpg","credit":"Superbass","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Turkey","place":"Istanbul, Turkey","at":[41.0064,28.9759],"text":"A night in a Turkish jail.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg/500px-Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","page":"Istanbul","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Iraq","place":"Baghdad, Iraq","at":[33.3062,44.3872],"text":"Across the desert, dodging bandits.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/5628442718_b10fc2c47f_o.jpg/500px-5628442718_b10fc2c47f_o.jpg","page":"Baghdad","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:5628442718_b10fc2c47f_o.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Khyber Pass","place":"Khyber Pass","at":[34.0786,71.2096],"text":"Almost shot at by Pashtun tribesmen.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/KhyberPassPakistan.jpg/500px-KhyberPassPakistan.jpg","page":"Khyber Pass","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KhyberPassPakistan.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"India","place":"Delhi, India","at":[28.6328,77.2198],"text":"Guest of rajahs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Jama_Masjid_2011.jpg/500px-Jama_Masjid_2011.jpg","page":"Delhi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jama_Masjid_2011.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Tokyo","place":"Tokyo, Japan","at":[35.6769,139.7639],"date":"1933","text":"The end, with the film that became his lecture tour.","by":"unknown","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Skyscrapers_of_Shinjuku_2009_January.jpg/500px-Skyscrapers_of_Shinjuku_2009_January.jpg","page":"Tokyo","source":"https: